  "definition": "t=0 follows target attainment and contains the post-wound transplant. Donor hidden values are copied from the same mature state with a rigid spatial rotation, aligning outward directions and attachment points; no resizing. Nearest-neighbor rasterization copies exact channel vectors but can change pixel counts. Freeze overrides global restore for updates 1..freeze_steps. After release, Growing compares the original mature reference with donor hidden vectors in the graft footprint only; the reference outside that footprint remains the original mature state. Persistent has no restore. RGBA composites are evaluation references only, never interventions; regime flags refer to the original target. Planaria uses equal-length thirds along the target's longitudinal axis; head at its upper end."
